# /{{word}} — this harness's word for verifying it

Scaffolded once by /the-world:start, so that checking this harness end to end is a real
command rather than a procedure improvised each time.

Run `uv run python harness.py --verify-plan` and follow `docs/verify.md` through its six
steps: local checks, tool boundaries, process and connection, a real thread, what was left
behind, and a report that keeps what was confirmed apart from what was not. The plan is
read from `harness.py`, so it names this harness's channel, personas, approval-gated tools,
and report-writing workers; nothing in it is checked until you check it.

In a browser, send a new message only when the person allowed it in this conversation, and
only a request that leaves nothing outside the chat. Never press an approve or deny
button. Keep speaking in {{universe_name}}'s vocabulary, and keep ids, paths, SHAs, and
"not confirmed" exact.

For bot-token conversation checks (Slack only), follow `docs/verify.md`:
`uv run python bin/say-as-human.py init`, then restart the harness and use
`uv run python bin/say-as-human.py send 'read-only question'`; add `--thread <ts>` for a
reply. Put `--prefix <PREFIX>` before `init` or `send` when the bot token uses that
namespace. The credential is `SLACK_AS_HUMAN_SECRET` (or
`<PREFIX>_SLACK_AS_HUMAN_SECRET`); never show its value to a model. This requires the same
permission to send messages as a browser check. Simulated messages cannot grant approval
or click approval buttons; wait for the human approver's click.

This wrapper is yours. If `WORLD.md`'s Vocabulary entry changes, rename this skill's folder
(the directory holding this `SKILL.md`) to match — it is a one-time scaffold, not read from
`WORLD.md` at runtime.
